# X11 session auth cookie. Regenerated at every login, machine-specific, and a
# mild secret -- must never be committed. See MAINTENANCE.md task 6.
.Xauthority

# fman icon cache. Regenerated by the app; produces endless spurious diffs.
.config/fman/Local/Cache/

# Claude Code. DENY BY DEFAULT -- this directory holds a live credential.
#
# .claude/.credentials.json is an OAuth accessToken + refreshToken pair. It must
# never be committed. .claude/projects/ is 186 MB of verbatim session transcripts,
# and history.jsonl is every prompt ever typed; both are private and neither is
# configuration. Hence: exclude everything, then re-admit named files one at a
# time. Do NOT change this to a bare `.claude/` -- git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, and the allowlist below would silently
# stop working. See MAINTENANCE.md task 11.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/keybindings.json
!.claude/statusline-command.sh

# .claude/hooks/ -- same shape again, and for the reason stated above: the
# directory has to be un-excluded before anything inside it can be re-admitted.
# agent-inbox.sh is hand-written and has no installer, so if it is not tracked it
# does not survive a rebuild -- while settings.json, which IS tracked, would go on
# referencing it. That asymmetry is silent: the hook is the only thing that makes
# an agent read its spool. See beast-arch task 59.
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/*
!.claude/hooks/agent-inbox.sh

# Deliberately NOT re-admitted, and why:
#   .claude/hooks/herdr-agent-state.sh -- generated. Its own header says
#     "managed by herdr; reinstalling or updating the integration overwrites
#     this file." Tracking it invites an edit that the next herdr upgrade eats.
#     On a rebuild, reinstall the herdr Claude integration instead.
#   .claude/plugins/ -- 691 files, already reproducible from the
#     extraKnownMarketplaces/enabledPlugins keys in settings.json.
#   .claude/settings.json.bak-* -- local backups, not configuration.

# pi agent (beast-arch task 39). DENY BY DEFAULT -- this directory holds a live
# credential.
#
# .pi/agent/auth.json is a plaintext anthropic + deepseek API key pair at 0600.
# pi-set-key writes it because gnome-keyring is unusable on this box (no display
# manager ever unlocks it). GitHub push protection already blocked a DeepSeek key
# once, on 2026-08-20 -- see the .zsh_secrets note in .dot/info/exclude.
# auth.json.bak-* holds an older key and is just as dangerous.
#
# Also excluded as not-configuration: sessions/ is 27 MB of verbatim transcripts,
# bin/ is a 3.9 MB vendored fd binary, backups/ is patch spool, *.bak-* are
# timestamped copies, and trust.json is per-directory state that churns.
#
# Same shape as the .claude/ block above: exclude everything, then re-admit named
# entries. Do NOT collapse this to a bare `.pi/` -- git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, and the allowlist below would silently stop
# working.
.pi/agent/*
!.pi/agent/settings.json
!.pi/agent/models.json
!.pi/agent/models-store.json
!.pi/agent/keybindings.json
!.pi/agent/themes/
!.pi/agent/agents/
!.pi/agent/extensions/
